## 3.10 Syntax to settle before the first tag
Grammar changes are cheap now and costly once other people have notes.
- [ ] Labels: a plain `Text:` is a label only up to 3 words (almost every label is 1-3); longer labels opt in with `*A longer label like this one:*`, parsed at the same level as plain labels. Lua and Go parsers, `tests/fixtures/ast`, Syntax.md; first a command that lists the lines whose kind would change, and check `*…:*` against emphasis spans (Wishlist # 8) @p2 @size(md)
- [ ] Tag search filters with `is:` words (a colon can't be in a tag, so they can't clash): `@[rust is:heading]`, `@[rl is:open]`, `@[rust is:task, rust is:label]`; kinds `heading label item task open done resource`. `@[#-:/tags]` would collide with the scope, which is a link (Wishlist # 8) @p2 @size(md)

# 5 Next (agreed 2026-10-16)
Details in Wishlist # 8.

## 5.1 Calendar and planning
- [ ] Inbox triage: `@project(1.4)` on an inbox item or loose task; the daily review lists them with `m` to move each to its project, and items without one to `review.inbox_default` (a place in the projects note, e.g. a heading of `[P/#Areas]`, the area tree for maintenance tasks that aren't projects) @p2 @size(md)
- [ ] Project blocks: a calendar line holding only a project link, with nothing under it, shows the project's next open tasks (`ui.planner.project_tasks`) as references, toggling the tasks (Neovim calendar view and web) @p3 @size(md)
- [ ] Help: one table of the keys of each zortex buffer and picker, so `?`, README, `:help zortex-keys` and the picker titles come from it; mention each picker backend's own help key @p3 @size(sm)

## 5.2 Links and tags
- [ ] A `-` component matches a task's `@id` too: `[P/-aB3x9]` keeps pointing at a task through renames (no new link component for tasks) @p3 @size(sm)
- [ ] Notes outside `notes_dir` (a repo's `doc/Roadmap.zortex`): their links resolve in their own folder; `[~/P/#Subaru]` reaches `notes_dir` @p3 @size(md)
- [ ] Broken and orphan tags, computed on request: tag searches that find nothing, `[@Tag]` links to a tag no note has, and bare tags no search uses (bare attributes like `@p1` left out); `/broken` lists them apart from broken links, Neovim through `:ZortexBrokenLinks` @p3 @size(md)

## 5.3 Web
- [ ] Hover cards on links: a note's title, path, tags, first lines and backlink count; an image's thumbnail; an external link's domain and URL (nothing fetched from the server) @p3 @size(md)
- [ ] Graph: a note's headings that other notes link to, under the note: the structure as it actually grows @p3 @size(md)

## 5.4 XP
- [ ] Area split: keep the harmonic default; `xp.area_split` sets a geometric ratio instead (1: even, 0.7: gently decaying) @p3 @size(sm)
- [ ] Wording: "1 XP = 6 minutes of estimated work" wherever XP is shown or documented, and hours next to XP @p3 @size(sm)

Dropped: a raw-text section, uploading a file to render it, tags generated from Structure, other rules for a tagged heading's rows, XP "overlap", the calendar picker.

# 4 After v0.1.0
- [ ] Tree-sitter grammar with the AST fixtures as acceptance tests (Wishlist # 7) @size(xl)
- [x] LazyVim defaults: blink.cmp source next to the nvim-cmp one; pickers behind one interface with snacks.picker and fzf-lua backends next to telescope (`ui.picker = "auto"`) @size(lg) @done(2026-10-15)
- [ ] Web app as an installable PWA (phone + Syncthing): the first thing after v0.1.0 @p1 @size(md)
- [x] Pomodoro sessions into the calendar / XP (log what a session was spent on): time tracking writes @spent @size(md) @done(2026-10-12)
- [ ] Import from Markdown / Obsidian vaults @size(lg)

Decisions:
- One repo, one version: the plugin and `zortex serve` are tagged together (decided 2026-10-16).
- Platforms promised: Linux and macOS; Windows untested (README, decided 2026-10-14).
- Names: `zortex.nvim` for the plugin, `zortex` for the binary and the image on ghcr.io (`ghcr.io/t-wilkinson/zortex`, decided 2026-10-16).
- Notifications: every timed calendar line notifies (keeps you on track, pulls you out of deep focus); `@n(no)` opts a line out, `@event` marks the fixed things you plan around (decided 2026-10-16).
